# Deployment template only: adjust paths to the actual host installation.
# Resolve all failed --check items before deployment. Read-only checks return
# preflight_required while actual SQLite write/atomic commit and runtime probes
# remain unverified; they never certify transactional readiness.
# API: docker run --mount type=bind,src=/home/lxc/chip-recommend/data,dst=/app/data ...
DATA_DB_PATH=/home/lxc/chip-recommend/data/data.db
AISH_PERF_CONTAINER_DATA_ROOT=/app/data
AISH_PERF_API_CONTAINER=chip-recommend
HERMES_CLI_COMMAND=/usr/local/lib/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes
HERMES_PYTHON=/usr/local/lib/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python
AISH_PERF_HERMES_SKILL_ROOT=/home/lxc/.hermes/skills
# Optional SDK source path, if required by the actual Hermes installation:
# HERMES_SDK_ROOT=/usr/local/lib/hermes-agent
# Set credentials explicitly in your private EnvironmentFile, never in this template.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# HERMES_MODEL=
# HERMES_PROVIDER=
# Admin token lives in shared data/manual_control/admin_token, not in request bodies.
# V3 tools use an authenticated ephemeral host loopback endpoint for each run.
# Legacy port 5341 is not a V3 capability and requires no forwarding into Docker.
# CLI --db chosen.db uses the resolved database parent as shared --data-root.
# Bind that same directory into Docker; configured API DATA_DB_PATH may use
# /app/data/chosen.db. Only the relative chosen.db locator is persisted.
# Resume without --db inherits its original source; changing it is rejected.
# Old requests without a saved locator require a new run, never default data.db.
